entityDescription:
Sofiyska Voda JSC provides water and wastewater services on the territory of the Municipality of Sofia for more than 1 400 000 citizens. It is the largest water utility company in Bulgaria. It is in charge of managing the whole water cycle: treatment and distribution of drinking water, collection and treatment of wastewater for the city of Sofia and its surrounding areas. 
Sofiyska Voda JSC is a joint-stock company established on 6 October 2000 under a 25 years concession contract for the water supply and sewerage system on the territory of Sofia Municipality. 
The shareholders of the company are Sofia Municipality (22.9% of the shares) and Veolia (the majority shareholder of 77.1% of the shares).
About 1200 people are working for the company, of which 60 percent are engineers or exercise a profession related to the operation and maintenance of the WSS system.
The activities of Sofiyska voda JSC include the operation, maintenance and management of 3725 km of water mains and 1733 km of sewers through an asset base including:
- 2 Wastewater treatment plants; 
- 4 Wastewater pumping stations;
- 4 Potable water treatment plants;
- 51 Reservoirs;
- 21 Water pumping stations;
- 39 Chlorination stations
